Third-party material in this repository

- assets/so101: SO-101 robot model from MuJoCo Menagerie (robotstudio_so101), Apache License 2.0.
  The license text is kept at assets/so101/LICENSE. The simulation timestep in so101.xml was
  changed from 0.005 to 0.002. web/public/assets/so101 holds a derived copy with decimated
  visual meshes.
- MuJoCo (native `mujoco` and the `@mujoco/mujoco` WebAssembly build), Apache License 2.0.
- three.js, MIT License.
- The browser teleoperation app was designed after Axis Robotics' open AxisWebInfra
  (Apache License 2.0, https://github.com/AxisAIOrg/AxisWebInfra). No source code from that
  repository was copied: it targets a Franka arm, an older mujoco-js build and Next.js, none of
  which fit this project's requirement of one exact MuJoCo version in browser and validator.

- The landing arm joint poses and visual transforms were adapted
  from the user-provided awign-hackathon-2026/frontend project. The arm uses this repository's
  existing SO-101 decimated meshes; its license is also included in web/public/assets/so101/LICENSE.
- The landing reference film and derived poster came from Axis Robotics at the user's direction
  (https://axisrobotics.ai/media/bottleneck-card-2.mp4). Attribution appears in the site footer.
